From beb0472a808129bec21d7665e068bd85d2df2cda Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zak Wilson <zak.wilson@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 09:29:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] cheader: read RET (name)(args); defvar arrays of a header
 struct

Two fixes found by the nuc-lua port.

ISSUE-002: lua.h declares every API function as `int (lua_gettop)
(lua_State *L);` so that a function-like macro of the same name can't
expand there. The importer skipped all 157. One pair of parentheses
around the name is now read; `int ((f))(int);` stays the canonical
unread shape, and s16-c2-skip-reason-recorded now uses it.

ISSUE-003: `(defvar regs:(array luaL_Reg 3) ...)` was refused as an
array of an opaque type: the provisional prescan resolves the element
before the header's layout is in, and checked opacity first.

Test: lua-header-shapes in tests/suite-cimport.nuc.
Gate: 1737 passed, 0 failed; bootstrap fixed point holds.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CsC8i2S7yJAHSpzRaddMj3
